
## Path Fixtures

Path fixtures in Lappa are defined in meters with the origin at the bottom-left corner of the simulation environment. This ensures consistency across different simulations and makes it easier to interpret and compare results.

### Example Path Fixture

```json
{
  "waypoints": [
    {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.0},
    {"x": 1.5, "y": 8.0},
    {"x": 1.5, "y": 0.0},
    {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.0}
  ]
}
```

In this example, the robot starts at the origin `(0.0, 0.0)`, drives up the aisle to `(0.0, 8.0)`, strafes across to `(1.5, 8.0)`, drives back down to `(1.5, 0.0)`, and finally strafes back to the start `(0.0, 0.0)`.

### Origin Conventions

- The origin `(0.0, 0.0)` is located at the bottom-left corner of the simulation environment.
- Coordinates are defined in meters.
- The x-axis points to the right, and the y-axis points upwards.

